table_index; get_context_records gives Context\nrecords. get_source_context, get_gds_context and get_objects repeat inline data; do not\ncall them.\n\nReaders return items with next_cursor/is_complete. Continue a chain with the returned\ncursor alone; a null selector (omit it instead), a selector added to a cursor, another\nreader's cursor, an unknown key or malformed arguments fail the whole run. Each call\nuses one of limited turns (default 50 per attempt) and each page stays in context;\nexhausting either fails the run. A reply without a reader call is your final answer, so\nfinish every read first. A repair attempt starts without earlier reader results; re-read\nwhat fixes need.",
    "instruction_prompt": "Optimize the whole Logical model from inline and reader evidence with the ordered design\nabove and the final checks below.\n\n## Authoring settings\nnaming_instructions: {{ naming_instructions }}\nschemas: {{ schemas }}\nlogical_entity_scd_type: {{ logical_entity_scd_type }}\naudit_columns: {{ audit_columns }}\nlogical_entity_types: {{ logical_entity_types }}\ntable_index: {{ table_index }}\n\n## Evidence\nmodel_summary: {{ model_summary }}\nunlinked_analysis_edges: {{ unlinked_analysis_edges }}\ntype_conflicts: {{ type_conflicts }}\nname_variants: {{ name_variants }}\nentity_details: {{ entity_details }}\n\n## Final checks\nBefore returning, confirm: every change answers a finding or clear evidence; every merge\nkeeps one Entity, moves its sources, Attributes and Relationships and retires the other;\nevery Relationship names an existing foreign-key Attribute and parent Entity; no locked\nrecord changes; every table id and column exists in table_index.",
